  },
  data: {
    LLM: '1. Standard Play: Follow Podkidnoy rules (Attacking, Defending, Throw-ins).\n2. Initial Trump: Use the face-up card suit for the first phase.\n3. The Shift: When the stock is empty, the player who draws the LAST (face-down) card reveals it.\n4. New Reality: The suit of that final card IMMEDIATELY becomes the new trump suit for the rest of the game.',
    Player: '1. Standard Play: Follow Podkidnoy rules (Attacking, Defending, Throw-ins).\n2. Initial Trump: Use the face-up card suit for the first phase.\n3. The Shift: When the stock is empty, the player who draws the LAST (face-down) card reveals it.\n4. New Reality: The suit of that final card IMMEDIATELY becomes the new trump suit for the rest of the game.',
    objective: "Escape the 'Fool' (Durak) title by shedding all cards, especially during the chaotic trump-shift endgame.",
    gameplay: '1. Standard Play: Follow Podkidnoy rules (Attacking, Defending, Throw-ins).\n2. Initial Trump: Use the face-up card suit for the first phase.\n3. The Shift: When the stock is empty, the player who draws the LAST (face-down) card reveals it.\n4. New Reality: The suit of that final card IMMEDIATELY becomes the new trump suit for the rest of the game.',
    keyRules: [
      'The change of trump suit happens instantly; currently active attacks are resolved using the NEW suit.',
      "If the face-down card matches the initial trump suit, nothing changes (a 'lucky North').",
      'Standard attack limits (6 cards) apply.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
